### Test the REST API from inside VS Code
### Install the "REST Client" extension, start the backend, then click "Send Request" above each block.

@base = http://localhost:8080/api/students

### READ all students
GET {{base}}

### READ with search
GET {{base}}?search=computer

### READ one student
GET {{base}}/1

### CREATE a student  (201 Created)
POST {{base}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Kiran Rao",
  "email": "kiran.rao@college.edu",
  "rollNo": "CS2099",
  "department": "Computer Science",
  "yearOfStudy": 2
}

### UPDATE a student
PUT {{base}}/1
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Asha Reddy",
  "email": "asha.reddy@college.edu",
  "rollNo": "CS2041",
  "department": "Information Technology",
  "yearOfStudy": 3
}

### DELETE a student  (204 No Content)
DELETE {{base}}/2

### Validation error example  (400 Bad Request)
POST {{base}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "",
  "email": "not-an-email",
  "rollNo": "x",
  "department": "CSE",
  "yearOfStudy": 7
}
